    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0252" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg138"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4272: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Edge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-04T15:00:00+01:00">July 4, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 4—11:56 a.m.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d90-f1"
                        />]</dateline></opener>
                <p>404. The following is the question discussed by Mr. Mellon with Mr. Mills at
                    2:30.</p>
                <p>We are assured by M. Flandin, the Minister of Finance, that the French Government
                    will agree to the 12-year repayment period if the American Government will state
                    that if an agreement can be reached between France, Germany and the other
                    interested powers on the continuation of the deliveries in kind for the year
                    1931–1932, it will interpose no objection.</p>
                <p>We understand from M. Flandin that the total of these payments is 250 million
                    reichsmarks but all but 120 million had already been contracted for and financed
                    which means that the German budget in the coming year only would be affected to
                    the extent of 30 million dollars which could be financed internally over a
                    longer period by the Government of the Reich to its own national[s].</p>
                <p>A favorable answer would remove all existing questions as per your 329<anchor
                        n="25" xml:id="d90-f2"/> which are capable of settlement between the United
                    States and France and make an agreement in principle possible tonight.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
